.TH CPU-NIGHT-MODE 1 "October 2026" "cpu-night-mode 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
cpu-night-mode \- scheduled, reversible CPU frequency ceilings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpu-night-mode
.RI [ flags ] " command"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies a maximum frequency to every CPUFreq policy during a daily time window.
Original ceilings are saved before writes and restored outside the window or
when the systemd service stops. The default window is 19:00 to 09:00 in
Europe/Berlin with a 1600 MHz ceiling. Evaluation occurs every 30 seconds.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Run the scheduler. Normally started by cpu-night-mode.service as root.
.TP
.B status
Print the on-disk configuration, current policy ceilings, and recovery state.
.TP
.B check-config
Validate configuration without changing hardware.
.TP
.B restore
Restore saved policy ceilings. Run as root with the daemon stopped.
Does not require a valid configuration file.
.TP
.B version
Print the program version.
.SH FLAGS
Flags must precede the command.
.TP
.BI -config " path"
Configuration file (default /etc/cpu-night-mode.conf).
.TP
.BI -sysfs " path"
CPUFreq policy root (default /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq).
.TP
.BI -state-dir " path"
Recovery directory (default /run/cpu-night-mode).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The INI file supports schedule.start and schedule.end in HH:MM format,
schedule.timezone as an IANA timezone, and cpu.max_frequency_mhz as an integer.
Start is inclusive, end exclusive; equal times are invalid. Omitted settings
use defaults. Unknown or duplicate keys are errors.
.PP
Validate with cpu-night-mode check-config, then use
sudo systemctl reload cpu-night-mode to apply edits.
Invalid configuration on reload retains the previous configuration.
.SH RECOVERY
sudo systemctl stop cpu-night-mode restores the original limits.
sudo systemctl disable --now cpu-night-mode also disables automatic startup.
Failed restoration retains originals.json for a subsequent recovery attempt.
systemd ExecStopPost runs recovery after crashes, including SIGKILL.
.SH FILES
.TP
/etc/cpu-night-mode.conf
Configuration, preserved on package upgrades.
.TP
/run/cpu-night-mode/originals.json
Original per-policy ceilings and current boot ID.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
